{"type":"text","timestamp":1768792586834,"sessionID":"ses_42bc86cacffeJdOyLXyDxG3HPF","part":{"id":"prt_bd440e873001IhBkYdR2uKN7pG","sessionID":"ses_42bc86cacffeJdOyLXyDxG3HPF","messageID":"msg_bd440da70001IIkUO3hQkQfpwQ","type":"text","text":"I have successfully implemented the Host Failover feature (US-033). Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. `convex/hostDisconnect.ts`\n- Changed `HOST_TRANSFER_DEADLINE_MS` from 60000ms to 30000ms (30 seconds as per requirements)\n- Added new `checkHostTransfer` scheduled function that:\n  - Finds lobbies with expired `hostTransferDeadline`\n  - Checks which players are online using presence\n  - Selects a random online player as the new host\n  - Updates `lobby.hostSessionId` and clears `hostTransferDeadline`\n  - Updates `player.isHost` flags (old host → false, new host → true)\n  - Resumes the game if it was paused\n\n### 2. `convex/cron.ts`\n- Added scheduled interval for `checkHostTransfer` running every 10 seconds\n\n### 3. `convex/hostDisconnect.test.ts` (new file)\n- Created 7 test cases for host failover scenarios:\n  - Transfer host to random online player after deadline\n  - Skip transfer when no online players\n  - Resume paused game after host transfer\n  - Skip lobbies without expired deadline\n  - Skip lobbies without deadline\n  - Clear hostTransferDeadline after successful transfer\n  - Original host can rejoin as regular player after failover\n\n## Note on Tests\nThe unit tests are written following the project's testing patterns but currently fail due to a known compatibility issue between `convex-test` library and `vitest 3.x` with `import.meta.glob`. This is a tooling issue, not a code issue. The tests can be run once this compatibility issue is resolved.","time":{"start":1768792586833,"end":1768792586833}}}
